      "hints": [
        "Rearrange $y = (2x+3)^2 + 1$ to make $x$ the subject.",
        "The domain of $(fg)^{-1}$ is the range of $fg$ on $x > 0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = (2x + 3)^2 + 1$ and rearrange to isolate $(2x + 3)^2$:\n$$(2x + 3)^2 = y - 1$$",
        "Take the positive square root since $x > 0$ implies $2x + 3 > 3$:\n$$2x + 3 = \\sqrt{y - 1} \\implies 2x = \\sqrt{y - 1} - 3 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{y - 1} - \\frac{3}{2}$$",
        "Write the inverse function in terms of $x$:\n$$(fg)^{-1}(x) = \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x - 1} - \\frac{3}{2}$$",
        "Determine the domain of $(fg)^{-1}(x)$, which is the range of $fg(x)$ for $x > 0$:\n$$\\text{For } x > 0:\\quad fg(x) > (2(0) + 3)^2 + 1 = 10 \\implies \\text{Domain is } x > 10$$"
      ],
